{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3332","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3332","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3332\",\"parent_revision\":\"eba9b34524bcbf8f575633d91cfdd37bac5d62f4021244b3d42fdab7e9620e33\",\"root_revision\":\"eba9b34524bcbf8f575633d91cfdd37bac5d62f4021244b3d42fdab7e9620e33\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-29\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md` has two live consumers today \u2014 `agents/backlog-item-groomer.md`'s Output Format section and `skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-agent.md`'s dispatch prompt \u2014 and is about to gain a third via the `dh-meta-docs` skill index. Confirmed drift against `backlog_core/models.py`, verified directly:\\n\\n- `:15` documents a `name:` frontmatter field. `BacklogItem` has no such field \u2014 real fields are `title`/`reference`/`description` (`models.py:1011-1013`).\\n- `:5` \\\"Location\\\" framing says groomed content \\\"lives in the body of `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/backlog/{priority}-{slug}.md`\\\" \u2014 stale extension (real storage is `.yaml`, per `backlog_core/yaml_io.py:84`'s `save_item()` docstring: \\\"Always writes `.yaml` format regardless of the original file extension\\\"), and this framing doesn't apply at all to `sqlite`/`memory`/`beads` backends, which have no such file-path structure (per `AGENTS.md`'s Backend Providers section).\\n- `:23`'s status vocabulary example (`open|in-progress|done|resolved`) is inconsistent with the vocabulary used elsewhere in the codebase.\\n\\nGoal: correct the frontmatter field list and status vocabulary against `models.py` directly, and rewrite or remove the backend-specific \\\"Location\\\" framing so the doc states only the backend-agnostic content schema (frontmatter shape, body sections, Groomed subsections) that actually gets passed through `backlog_groom(groomed_content=...)` regardless of which backend is configured. This is actively misleading the grooming agent today, not a cosmetic issue.\\n\\nUser-provided context: surfaced while auditing plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/ for deletion, and while fixing a broken hook that pointed backlog-item-groomer.md at this doc via a nonexistent `.claude/docs/...` path \u2014 see #3329.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Follow-up from #3329 (dh:backlog dead-skill cleanup)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"9a67e7078467164d9fa32bac05411a7ed203da46c028dd29ef6bdfc814339633\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABReqMgg\"}"}